1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,875
If you take one thing away from this talk, make it this: the frontmatter is the most important part of the file.

2
00:00:04,825 --> 00:00:06,991
The name and description are not metadata.

3
00:00:06,991 --> 00:00:08,791
They are the routing mechanism.

4
00:00:08,791 --> 00:00:14,333
Before the agent reads a single line of your instructions, it looks at those two fields to decide: should I use this skill right now?

5
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:16,433
Most skill mistakes happen right here.

6
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:19,141
A vague description means the agent never triggers.

7
00:00:19,141 --> 00:00:23,950
Start with 'Use when', write it in third person, and describe the situation — not the solution.

